# 38. Synthetic Dataset Generation

Create a Python script:

```bash
python scripts/generate_training_data.py
```

It should generate query variations from the structured command dataset.

Use templates such as:

```text
how do I {intent}?
how can I {intent}?
what command {intent}?
command to {intent}
how to {intent}
{technology} {intent}
```

Do not rely on an LLM to generate the dataset.

Use deterministic templates initially.

Human-authored queries should be the highest-quality dataset.

